769
01:42:27.178 --> 01:42:30.178
And there the congregation of Philippi arises.

770
01:42:30.178 --> 01:42:33.178
And we do not know exactly who the pastor was.

771
01:42:33.178 --> 01:42:35.178
And how many people were in that church.

772
01:42:35.178 --> 01:42:37.178
But it is the church in Philippi.

773
01:42:37.178 --> 01:42:39.178
And what is so beautiful about this church.

774
01:42:39.178 --> 01:42:43.178
Is that this church fully received it.

775
01:42:43.178 --> 01:42:47.178
It says what we just read in Acts chapter 16.

776
01:42:48.178 --> 01:42:51.178
They listened to everything Paul said.

777
01:42:51.178 --> 01:42:53.178
And Paul is a pure source.

778
01:42:53.178 --> 01:42:56.178
Is a pure source of the gospel.

779
01:42:56.178 --> 01:42:59.178
At that time there were also many strange characters.

780
01:42:59.178 --> 01:43:01.178
Who went around with all sorts of stories.

781
01:43:01.178 --> 01:43:03.178
Gnosticism was on the rise.

782
01:43:03.178 --> 01:43:05.178
They were all gospel chatter.

783
01:43:05.178 --> 01:43:08.178
They were not gospel, they were false messages.

784
01:43:08.178 --> 01:43:12.178
But what Paul brought was the pure Word of God.

785
01:43:12.178 --> 01:43:15.178
And then Acts chapter 16 says.

786
01:43:15.178 --> 01:43:19.178
And Lydia listened to what Paul said.

787
01:43:19.178 --> 01:43:23.178
And there she came to repentance.

788
01:43:23.178 --> 01:43:29.178
So again, your repentance must happen on the pure gospel.

789
01:43:29.178 --> 01:43:32.178
Not on a prosperity gospel.

790
01:43:32.178 --> 01:43:36.178
Not on a you're-the-best-you gospel.

791
01:43:36.178 --> 01:43:39.178
Not on a low-threshold gospel.

792
01:43:39.178 --> 01:43:41.178
Vanessa and I were still talking about that.

793
01:43:41.178 --> 01:43:44.178
Why should we make the church low-threshold?

794
01:43:44.178 --> 01:43:47.178
The gospel is not low-threshold.

795
01:43:47.178 --> 01:43:49.178
Someone died for it on a cross.

796
01:43:49.178 --> 01:43:52.178
He was the Creator of heaven and earth Himself.

797
01:43:52.178 --> 01:43:55.178
Why should we make that sound easier?

798
01:43:55.178 --> 01:44:00.178
Not on that prosperity gospel or a charismatic movement.

799
01:44:00.178 --> 01:44:02.178
That throws around prophecies.

800
01:44:02.178 --> 01:44:05.178
And you will be this, and you will be that, and you will be such.

801
01:44:05.178 --> 01:44:08.178
And what if a storm comes all of a sudden.

802
01:44:08.178 --> 01:44:10.178
And it hasn't happened yet.

803
01:44:10.178 --> 01:44:12.178
What you have ever heard in your life.

804
01:44:12.178 --> 01:44:15.178
You will become this later.

805
01:44:15.178 --> 01:44:17.178
Yes, what then?

806
01:44:17.178 --> 01:44:19.178
And then it doesn't happen.

807
01:44:19.178 --> 01:44:22.178
And then just let it be then.

808
01:44:22.178 --> 01:44:24.178
But that is not the gospel.

809
01:44:24.178 --> 01:44:28.178
How often have you ever heard in the Western church?

810
01:44:28.178 --> 01:44:31.178
And you will die from beatings.

811
01:44:31.178 --> 01:44:34.178
And they will freeze your bank account.

812
01:44:34.178 --> 01:44:37.178
You don't hear that. Those are doom prophecies.

813
01:44:37.178 --> 01:44:40.178
But do you know that it is indeed in the Bible?

814
01:44:40.178 --> 01:44:44.178
Paul comes to repentance after he was Saul.

815
01:44:44.178 --> 01:44:48.178
And then he says, what is that name of the one who speaks to the Lord?

816
01:44:48.178 --> 01:44:51.178
What is his name? Who?

817
01:44:51.178 --> 01:44:54.178
Yes? Agabus?

818
01:44:54.178 --> 01:44:58.178
No, but the one who speaks to the Lord, isn't his name also Ananias?

819
01:44:58.178 --> 01:45:01.178
Ananias, right? Ananias then says to the Lord.

820
01:45:01.178 --> 01:45:04.178
Lord, do you know what you are doing?

821
01:45:04.178 --> 01:45:06.178
For this is Saul, who has the man.

822
01:45:06.178 --> 01:45:09.178
Do you know what the Lord says then? Beautiful prophecy.

823
01:45:09.178 --> 01:45:12.178
Oh, Ananias.

824
01:45:12.178 --> 01:45:15.178
Take good care of him, for you do not yet know half...

825
01:45:15.178 --> 01:45:18.178
how much he will have to suffer for the gospel.

826
01:45:18.178 --> 01:45:20.178
Suffering with a long 'ij'.

827
01:45:20.178 --> 01:45:22.178
Nothing millionaire.

828
01:45:22.178 --> 01:45:25.178
Nothing everyone will be happy with you.

829
01:45:25.178 --> 01:45:28.178
Nothing full churches. Nothing new buildings.

830
01:45:28.178 --> 01:45:32.178
No, a basement with concrete and beatings.

831
01:45:32.178 --> 01:45:35.178
That was for Paul. And do you know what Paul does?

832
01:45:35.178 --> 01:45:38.178
Worship, the almighty one.

833
01:45:38.178 --> 01:45:42.178
Because they were happy...

834
01:45:42.178 --> 01:45:47.178
that they had the honor to suffer like Jesus.

835
01:45:47.178 --> 01:45:51.178
Dear church, let us in 2025...

836
01:45:51.178 --> 01:45:55.178
have our faith in order, please.

837
01:45:55.178 --> 01:45:58.178
If there are still things you need to clean up...

838
01:45:58.178 --> 01:46:01.178
and lay at the cross, then do it.

839
01:46:01.178 --> 01:46:03.178
Lay it down at Jesus' feet.

840
01:46:03.178 --> 01:46:07.178
But let us have a real faith in King Jesus.

841
01:46:07.178 --> 01:46:10.178
And that said in Philippians chapter 1.

842
01:46:10.178 --> 01:46:13.178
And I will quickly go through it.

843
01:46:13.178 --> 01:46:16.178
For I want to inject five quick things in Philippians chapter 1...

844
01:46:16.178 --> 01:46:19.178
I will read through it quickly...

845
01:46:19.178 --> 01:46:21.178
and then I will tell you what I want to say.

846
01:46:21.178 --> 01:46:24.178
This letter is from Paul and Timothy, here I stand...

847
01:46:24.178 --> 01:46:27.178
servants of Jesus Christ.

848
01:46:27.178 --> 01:46:29.178
We send greetings to all the people in Philippi...

849
01:46:29.178 --> 01:46:33.178
who believe in Jesus Christ...

850
01:46:33.178 --> 01:46:36.178
and to their leaders.

851
01:46:36.178 --> 01:46:38.178
I pray that God, who is our Father...

852
01:46:38.178 --> 01:46:41.178
will be good to you in everything.

853
01:46:41.178 --> 01:46:44.178
And that you will be filled with the peace of God...

854
01:46:44.178 --> 01:46:47.178
the Father and of the Lord Jesus Christ.

855
01:46:47.178 --> 01:46:50.178
Dear church, can I get an amen on that?

856
01:46:50.178 --> 01:46:53.178
Okay, here is the first bullet point we are going to zoom in on.

857
01:46:53.178 --> 01:46:56.178
Every time I think of you...

858
01:46:56.178 --> 01:46:59.178
I thank God, says Paul.

859
01:46:59.178 --> 01:47:02.178
This is a happy letter.

860
01:47:02.178 --> 01:47:04.178


861
01:47:04.178 --> 01:47:08.178
Whenever I pray for you, I am glad about you.

862
01:47:08.178 --> 01:47:10.178
This is a happy letter.

863
01:47:10.178 --> 01:47:13.178
For you have believed the good news...

864
01:47:13.178 --> 01:47:17.178
from the very first day I explained it to Lydia.

865
01:47:17.178 --> 01:47:19.178
You have believed it.

866
01:47:19.178 --> 01:47:22.178
And look, what does it say?

867
01:47:22.178 --> 01:47:25.178
And you still believe it.

868
01:47:25.178 --> 01:47:29.178
How many people here in the room have been in Jesus for ten years?

869
01:47:29.178 --> 01:47:31.178
Ten years converted.

870
01:47:31.178 --> 01:47:35.178
How many people in the room have been converted for twenty years?

871
01:47:35.178 --> 01:47:37.178
Thirty years converted?

872
01:47:37.178 --> 01:47:39.178
Forty years converted?

873
01:47:39.178 --> 01:47:41.178
Wow, you are old.

874
01:47:41.178 --> 01:47:43.178
Fifty years converted?

875
01:47:45.178 --> 01:47:47.178
Who here has been converted the longest?

876
01:47:47.178 --> 01:47:50.178
Fifty years converted? Anyone fifty years converted?

877
01:47:50.178 --> 01:47:53.178
Where? Michiel, let's give a round of applause for Michiel.

878
01:47:53.178 --> 01:47:55.178
Great.

879
01:47:55.178 --> 01:47:59.178
And dad, how long have you been converted?

880
01:48:02.178 --> 01:48:04.178
A very long time.

881
01:48:04.178 --> 01:48:06.178
I love this guy.

882
01:48:10.178 --> 01:48:12.178
How many years?

883
01:48:13.178 --> 01:48:16.178
Sixty? Yes, that is still acceptable.

884
01:48:18.178 --> 01:48:20.178
Hans, really, I love you.

885
01:48:20.178 --> 01:48:22.178
Crown.

886
01:48:24.178 --> 01:48:26.178
I will say it one more time.

887
01:48:26.178 --> 01:48:29.178
And you still believe it.

888
01:48:29.178 --> 01:48:32.178
Hold on. Hold on.

889
01:48:32.178 --> 01:48:36.178
Do not let go. Do not dilute the gospel.

890
01:48:36.178 --> 01:48:39.178
Do not let this society dilute your faith.

891
01:48:39.178 --> 01:48:43.178
Do not let this society push you away with doubt.

892
01:48:43.178 --> 01:48:46.178
Do not let this society take you away from the faith.

893
01:48:46.178 --> 01:48:48.178
These are all tests.

894
01:48:48.178 --> 01:48:51.178
God tests your faith continuously.

895
01:48:51.178 --> 01:48:54.178
Day in and day out, your faith is tested.

896
01:48:54.178 --> 01:48:58.178
But you still believe it.

897
01:48:58.178 --> 01:49:01.178
Paul says to the open church.

898
01:49:01.178 --> 01:49:03.178
Let this be an open church letter.

899
01:49:03.178 --> 01:49:07.178
Lord, please, make us an open church or a Philadelphia church.

900
01:49:07.178 --> 01:49:08.178
Please.

901
01:49:08.178 --> 01:49:10.178
God is in you.

902
01:49:10.178 --> 01:49:12.178
This is the second lesson I want to share.

903
01:49:12.178 --> 01:49:15.178
God has begun a good work in you.

904
01:49:15.178 --> 01:49:21.178
And I am sure that he who has begun a good work in you,

905
01:49:21.178 --> 01:49:24.178
will also complete it.

906
01:49:25.178 --> 01:49:30.178
And that is why it is important for me to stand for a moment on that point

907
01:49:30.178 --> 01:49:36.178
that you need to go back and be critical and strict with yourself for a moment.

908
01:49:36.178 --> 01:49:39.178
Have I ever truly repented?

909
01:49:41.178 --> 01:49:43.178
Everyone focus for a moment.

910
01:49:43.178 --> 01:49:45.178
Have I ever truly repented?

911
01:49:45.178 --> 01:49:49.178
Because if your repentance has been real,

912
01:49:49.178 --> 01:49:53.178
not baptized out of family tradition,

913
01:49:53.178 --> 01:49:57.178
not baptized because I am now 16 and I think it's all nice

914
01:49:57.178 --> 01:50:02.178
and several teenagers are getting baptized, so I might as well get baptized too.

915
01:50:02.178 --> 01:50:06.178
Not because of any gospel at all,

916
01:50:06.178 --> 01:50:09.178
but has my faith been real,

917
01:50:09.178 --> 01:50:11.178
founded in Christ?

918
01:50:11.178 --> 01:50:14.178
Because for those people it applies,

919
01:50:14.178 --> 01:50:17.178
if he has begun a work in you,

920
01:50:17.178 --> 01:50:19.178
he will also complete it.

921
01:50:19.178 --> 01:50:21.178
For that storm is coming.

922
01:50:21.178 --> 01:50:23.178
And that crisis is coming.

923
01:50:23.178 --> 01:50:27.178
And even doing things wrong will also happen.

924
01:50:27.178 --> 01:50:30.178
Christians also make mistakes.

925
01:50:30.178 --> 01:50:33.178
But then you can say,

926
01:50:33.178 --> 01:50:36.178
Philippians chapter 1, verse 6,

927
01:50:50.178 --> 01:50:54.178
I know that tears fell down my cheeks and that I said to myself,

928
01:50:54.178 --> 01:50:57.178
Lord, if I continue like this, I will end up in hell.

929
01:50:57.178 --> 01:51:00.178
I want to come to you. I want to make you my Lord and Master.

930
01:51:00.178 --> 01:51:03.178
I know that my repentance has been a true repentance.

931
01:51:03.178 --> 01:51:05.178
No one can take that away from me.

932
01:51:05.178 --> 01:51:08.178
And after that, I made a thousand more mistakes.

933
01:51:08.178 --> 01:51:12.178
But I know that he who began a good work in me,

934
01:51:12.178 --> 01:51:14.178
will also complete it.

935
01:51:14.178 --> 01:51:17.178
For despite my failures,

936
01:51:17.178 --> 01:51:19.178
he can never fail me.

937
01:51:19.178 --> 01:51:21.178
For he is solid.

938
01:51:21.178 --> 01:51:23.178
He is the rock on which he can build.

939
01:51:23.178 --> 01:51:27.178
I may sometimes backtrack, three steps forward, two steps back.

940
01:51:27.178 --> 01:51:31.178
But together with Jesus, I just keep going. Amen?

941
01:51:31.178 --> 01:51:33.178
Amen.

942
01:51:35.178 --> 01:51:38.178
But I find it fair that you must be honest.

943
01:51:38.178 --> 01:51:43.178
I find it fair that you should not misuse this verse.

944
01:51:43.178 --> 01:51:48.178
I find it fair that if you have never truly come to repentance

945
01:51:48.178 --> 01:51:52.178
and are just a flimflammer in the faith,

946
01:51:52.178 --> 01:51:58.178
you should not pull this verse out of the closet as approval for your behavior.

947
01:51:58.178 --> 01:52:01.178
For that is not what Jesus is saying here.

948
01:52:01.178 --> 01:52:06.178
It is very obvious to me, verse 7, to think of you this way.

949
01:52:06.178 --> 01:52:11.178
That is because you and I love each other very much.

950
01:52:11.178 --> 01:52:15.178
For I know that the love of God that is in me is also in you.

951
01:52:15.178 --> 01:52:17.178
Ah, so lovely.

952
01:52:17.178 --> 01:52:23.178
For you are one with me, now that I am imprisoned and must defend myself before the emperor in Rome.

953
01:52:23.178 --> 01:52:25.178
No, that is not in Rome by the way.

954
01:52:25.178 --> 01:52:27.178
And I must explain what I believe exactly.

955
01:52:27.178 --> 01:52:29.178
This is indeed in Rome, sorry. This is the Philippians letter.

956
01:52:29.178 --> 01:52:31.178
This is one of the prison epistles.

957
01:52:31.178 --> 01:52:34.178
And I must explain what I believe exactly.

958
01:52:34.178 --> 01:52:40.178
God knows that I long to see you again with the love of Christ.

959
01:52:40.178 --> 01:52:45.178
I pray that your love will continue to grow.

960
01:52:45.178 --> 01:52:48.178
For through that, your wisdom will also grow.

961
01:52:48.178 --> 01:52:52.178
Then you will understand the things of God better and better.

962
01:52:52.178 --> 01:52:56.178
This is also a prayer of mine for myself.

963
01:52:56.178 --> 01:52:58.178
I want to keep growing.

964
01:52:58.178 --> 01:53:00.178
You cannot plateau.

965
01:53:00.178 --> 01:53:03.178
A plateau in Christ, that does not work.

966
01:53:03.178 --> 01:53:06.178
Heaven is there. That is the direction we are going.

967
01:53:06.178 --> 01:53:08.178
Do you understand what I mean? Symbolically what I am saying there.

968
01:53:08.178 --> 01:53:10.178
But you cannot plateau.

969
01:53:10.178 --> 01:53:13.178
Dear people who have been walking with Jesus for thirty, forty years.

970
01:53:13.178 --> 01:53:16.178
You cannot be comfortable in the gospel.

971
01:53:16.178 --> 01:53:19.178
Comfort is not promised in the gospel.

972
01:53:19.178 --> 01:53:23.178
It is towards Jesus or downwards.

973
01:53:23.178 --> 01:53:25.178
And if you think you are plateauing.

974
01:53:25.178 --> 01:53:28.178
Here is the guarantee. Then it goes in that direction.

975
01:53:28.178 --> 01:53:31.178
Yes, I have already read the Bible. Just give it a few months.

976
01:53:31.178 --> 01:53:32.178
I am busy right now.

977
01:53:32.178 --> 01:53:35.178
That is not plateauing. That is going down.

978
01:53:36.178 --> 01:53:39.178
Yes, I am too busy. Skipping church once.

979
01:53:41.178 --> 01:53:46.178
Yes, reading the Bible. I listen during the service.

980
01:53:47.178 --> 01:53:49.178
Do you understand what I mean?

981
01:53:49.178 --> 01:53:52.178
For Satan is defeated.

982
01:53:52.178 --> 01:53:57.178
But while he is falling down, he is still quite powerful in his grip to take people with him.

983
01:53:57.178 --> 01:54:01.178
He won't catch me, for I know I must be here.

984
01:54:01.178 --> 01:54:04.178
Oh, hallelujah.

985
01:54:04.178 --> 01:54:06.178
Which verse am I on?

986
01:54:06.178 --> 01:54:08.178
Ten, right?

987
01:54:08.178 --> 01:54:12.178
You will increasingly see which things are truly important.

988
01:54:12.178 --> 01:54:14.178
Underline this verse in your Bible.

989
01:54:14.178 --> 01:54:18.178
You will increasingly see which things are important.

990
01:54:18.178 --> 01:54:21.178
A lot of things are simply not important.

991
01:54:21.178 --> 01:54:23.178
A lot of things just don't matter.

992
01:54:23.178 --> 01:54:25.178
But Jesus does matter.

993
01:54:25.178 --> 01:54:29.178
As a result, you will be pure and perfect on the day that Christ returns.

994
01:54:29.178 --> 01:54:31.178
See? Jesus is coming back.

995
01:54:31.178 --> 01:54:37.178
I want to show you how God has changed you since He has acquitted you of guilt.

996
01:54:37.178 --> 01:54:41.178
And all of that thanks to Jesus Christ.

997
01:54:41.178 --> 01:54:46.178
As a result, people will honor and praise God.

998
01:54:46.178 --> 01:54:52.178
I'll quickly jump. Here we go, reading verse 12, verse 21, and verse 27.

999
01:54:52.178 --> 01:54:54.178
Verse 12.

1000
01:55:01.178 --> 01:55:07.178
If it has happened to me, the good news has spread even further.

1001
01:55:07.178 --> 01:55:17.178
My lesson to you is, no matter what happens, if you lay it at Jesus' feet, He can do amazing things with it.

1002
01:55:17.178 --> 01:55:21.178
For He is Lord over all.

1003
01:55:21.178 --> 01:55:34.178
And He has used Paul more powerfully because Satan struck him, stoned him, and locked him in concrete blocks.

1004
01:55:34.178 --> 01:55:38.178
And ultimately, he is here imprisoned for two years in Rome.

1005
01:55:38.178 --> 01:55:41.178
And he is still allowed to write letters in Rome.

1006
01:55:41.178 --> 01:55:46.178
And he writes four of those amazing prison letters.

1007
01:55:46.178 --> 01:55:51.178
And to this day, people are baptized in the name of Jesus.

1008
01:55:51.178 --> 01:55:53.178
Who Paul was allowed to speak to.

1009
01:55:53.178 --> 01:55:56.178
Why? In whatever situation you find yourself.

1010
01:55:56.178 --> 01:56:03.178
If you do it together with Jesus, He has the leverage for His glory.

1011
01:56:03.178 --> 01:56:08.178
So do not look at your situation, dear church. Look to Jesus.

1012
01:56:08.178 --> 01:56:12.178
Verse 21. For Paul has experienced everything.

1013
01:56:12.178 --> 01:56:19.178
And then Paul says in verse 21, to live means for me to live for Christ.

1014
01:56:19.178 --> 01:56:24.178
But if I die, it means something much better.

1015
01:56:24.178 --> 01:56:27.178
For then I am with the Lord.

1016
01:56:27.178 --> 01:56:31.178
All you English people, how do you say that in the English translation?

1017
01:56:31.178 --> 01:56:35.178
To live is Christ and to die is gain.

1018
01:56:35.178 --> 01:56:37.178
That's a beautiful one, huh?

1019
01:56:37.178 --> 01:56:41.178
To live is Christ and to die is gain.

1020
01:56:41.178 --> 01:56:43.178
If I live, I live for the Lord.

1021
01:56:43.178 --> 01:56:46.178
If I live, I do not live for my career.

1022
01:56:46.178 --> 01:56:48.178
I do not live for money.

1023
01:56:48.178 --> 01:56:51.178
I do not live to fulfill some prophecy.

1024
01:56:51.178 --> 01:56:53.178
I do not live for this and I do not live for that.

1025
01:56:53.178 --> 01:56:56.178
I live very simply for Jesus.

1026
01:56:56.178 --> 01:56:59.178
And when I die, I will go to Jesus.

1027
01:56:59.178 --> 01:57:01.178
Ideal, right?

1028
01:57:01.178 --> 01:57:05.178
And then, if you believe that, if you hold on to that, dear Philippian church of mine,

1029
01:57:05.178 --> 01:57:09.178
dear open church, if you hold on to that,

1030
01:57:09.178 --> 01:57:12.178
as long as I live for Jesus, I live for Him.

1031
01:57:12.178 --> 01:57:14.178
And when I die, I will go to Him.

1032
01:57:14.178 --> 01:57:16.178
Then nothing can happen.

1033
01:57:16.178 --> 01:57:20.178
Oh, wonderful. Then we Christians can be stubborn in our faith.

1034
01:57:20.178 --> 01:57:21.178
Wonderful.

1035
01:57:21.178 --> 01:57:25.178
Shall we stand? I will do verse 27.

1036
01:57:26.178 --> 01:57:29.178
Shall we stand? We will close with prayer.

1037
01:57:29.178 --> 01:57:32.178
And I want to speak this Bible verse over us,

1038
01:57:32.178 --> 01:57:35.178
because Paul has an instruction.

1039
01:57:37.178 --> 01:57:39.178
Everyone stand up, just for a moment. Hop, hop, hop.

1040
01:57:41.178 --> 01:57:44.178
Okay, last minute. Then I will pray for you.

1041
01:57:45.178 --> 01:57:51.178
Paul begins Philippians chapter 1 with a lot of encouragement.

1042
01:57:51.178 --> 01:57:53.178
You are doing well.

1043
01:57:53.178 --> 01:57:55.178
You believe in me. You have believed it.

1044
01:57:55.178 --> 01:57:57.178
You still believe it.

1045
01:57:57.178 --> 01:57:59.178
And now he gives an instruction.

1046
01:57:59.178 --> 01:58:02.178
And this instruction is not a warning, is not an angry instruction,

1047
01:58:02.178 --> 01:58:08.178
but this instruction is precisely to continue with what they are already doing.

1048
01:58:08.178 --> 01:58:11.178
Do you understand? And that is verse 27.

1049
01:58:11.178 --> 01:58:18.178
But you must live in a manner worthy of the good news of Christ.

1050
01:58:18.178 --> 01:58:21.178
It should not matter whether I come to you or stay here.

1051
01:58:21.178 --> 01:58:27.178
And it says here, I want to hear from you that you are one with each other.

1052
01:58:27.178 --> 01:58:29.178
Such a beautiful message, unity.

1053
01:58:29.178 --> 01:58:36.178
And that you strive together for the faith in the good news.

1054
01:58:36.178 --> 01:58:38.178
Shall we close our eyes?

1055
01:58:40.178 --> 01:58:42.178
Lord, I want to pray for open church.

1056
01:58:43.178 --> 01:58:47.178
Lord, I want, while I have my eyes closed,

1057
01:58:47.178 --> 01:58:51.178
to see us as a group standing before the throne of God.

1058
01:58:51.178 --> 01:58:53.178
As a church.

1059
01:58:53.178 --> 01:58:57.178
And I just want to say, Lord, look at us.

1060
01:58:58.178 --> 01:59:00.178
And search open church.

1061
01:59:02.178 --> 01:59:04.178
And let us see, Lord,

1062
01:59:05.178 --> 01:59:10.178
what rewards and commendations you pronounce over us.

1063
01:59:11.178 --> 01:59:16.178
Lord, let us also see what instructions you give to open church.

1064
01:59:18.178 --> 01:59:24.178
As open church collectively, together and to all people individually.

1065
01:59:24.178 --> 01:59:30.178
Holy Spirit, with my eyes closed I visualize you moving through the hall.

1066
01:59:30.178 --> 01:59:32.178
That you move through the hearts.

1067
01:59:32.178 --> 01:59:35.178
And I want to ask you to search us, Lord.

1068
01:59:36.178 --> 01:59:38.178
We want to make you proud, Lord.

1069
01:59:38.178 --> 01:59:40.178
We want to make you happy.

1070
01:59:40.178 --> 01:59:42.178
We want for your life, King Jesus.

1071
01:59:43.178 --> 01:59:46.178
Lord, if there are instructions.

1072
01:59:46.178 --> 01:59:48.178
Instructions of unity.

1073
01:59:48.178 --> 01:59:52.178
Instructions of perseverance in faith.

1074
01:59:53.178 --> 01:59:55.178
Instructions of coming to repentance.

1075
01:59:56.178 --> 02:00:01.178
Instructions of returning to that point of repentance where you were once converted.

1076
02:00:01.178 --> 02:00:05.178
But your flame has dimmed due to lack of oil.

1077
02:00:06.178 --> 02:00:08.178
Warnings even.

1078
02:00:08.178 --> 02:00:10.178
That you say, hey, it's now or never.

1079
02:00:10.178 --> 02:00:12.178
Come to me.

1080
02:00:12.178 --> 02:00:14.178
Repent of your sins.

1081
02:00:14.178 --> 02:00:16.178
Let yourself be cleansed by my blood.

1082
02:00:17.178 --> 02:00:19.178
Holy Spirit, I want to ask You.

1083
02:00:19.178 --> 02:00:22.178
Bless everyone in this room.

1084
02:00:22.178 --> 02:00:25.178
That we may persevere in faith in King Jesus.

1085
02:00:25.178 --> 02:00:27.178
That we may continue on.

1086
02:00:27.178 --> 02:00:33.178
In a unity that is founded on the Holy Gospel.

1087
02:00:33.178 --> 02:00:35.178
What Paul spoke in Philippians.

1088
02:00:35.178 --> 02:00:39.178
Namely that Jesus Christ is Lord.

1089
02:00:39.178 --> 02:00:42.178
And I bless us all, church, listen to these words.

1090
02:00:42.178 --> 02:00:46.178
I bless us for the coming days of this week.

1091
02:00:46.178 --> 02:00:51.178
That you may thoroughly gain perspective together with the Holy Spirit.

1092
02:00:51.178 --> 02:00:53.178
Where do I stand together with God?

1093
02:00:53.178 --> 02:00:58.178
And may the dear Lord Jesus guide me to new repentance.

1094
02:00:58.178 --> 02:01:00.178
In Jesus' mighty name.

1095
02:01:00.178 --> 02:01:02.178
And we all say amen.

1096
02:01:02.178 --> 02:01:05.178
Shall we give Him the glory and the honor. Amen.

1097
02:01:10.178 --> 02:01:13.178
Dear people, thank you all for coming to church.

1098
02:01:13.178 --> 02:01:15.178
That we could magnify the Lord together.

1099
02:01:15.178 --> 02:01:18.178
And we will see each other tomorrow, for tomorrow there is indeed prayer.

1100
02:01:18.178 --> 02:01:21.178
Half past seven. See you tomorrow, everyone. Bye bye.
